{
  "title": "Resting rate-pressure coupling does not reliably improve cross-sample DSST prediction beyond its components",
  "abstract": "In 1,265 NHANES 2011\u20132012 adults aged 60+ and 1,373 separately sampled 2013\u20132014 adults, adding source-centered systolic-pressure \u00d7 pulse coupling to flexible pressure/pulse and demographic predictors increased validation DSST MSE by 0.202779 score\u00b2 (0.126%). The source-refit/target-PSU 95% interval was [-1.355326, 2.765820]; source cross-validation also worsened. Reliable incremental prediction is not established.",
